{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e1c2a4-9f31-4d8a-8f10-pos0majdpay01",
    "name": "POS API - majdpay (dev)",
    "description": "POS endpoints of product-management-service.\n\nBuilt from:\n- pos-api-reference-business.md (self-service / tenant-scoped)\n- pos-api-reference-admin.md (back-office / unscoped)\n- pos-api-reference-integration.md (terminal callback)\n\nBase URL: https://gateway-dev.majdpay.com\n\nAll requests need: Authorization: Bearer {{token}} (set at collection level), device-finger-print, platform.\nEvery endpoint also needs its own privilege on the token - a valid token alone is not enough (403 UNAUTHORIZED_USER otherwise).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "https://gateway-dev.majdpay.com" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "deviceFingerPrint", "value": "" },
    { "key": "platform", "value": "WEB" },
    { "key": "terminalId", "value": "T0012345" },
    { "key": "walletReference", "value": "WLT-0099" },
    { "key": "walletCode", "value": "WLT-0099" },
    { "key": "profileCode", "value": "PRF-0123" },
    { "key": "merchantId", "value": "123456789012" },
    { "key": "batchRef", "value": "BR-2026-08-30-001" },
    { "key": "batchRef2", "value": "BR-2026-08-30-002" },
    { "key": "stan", "value": "" },
    { "key": "rrn", "value": "" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Fresh STAN/RRN per run so callback requests are not treated as duplicates.",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('stan', String(Math.floor(Math.random() * 900000) + 100000));",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('rrn', String(Date.now()).slice(-12));"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Business (self-service, tenant-scoped)",
      "description": "Caller sees only their own data. Scoping comes from profileCode inside the JWT. Privileges: GET_POS_TRANSACTIONS, GET_POS_LEDGER.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. GET my transactions",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Spring Page envelope', () => {",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(b).to.have.property('content');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.content).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  pm.expect(b).to.have.property('totalElements');",
                  "});",
                  "const c = pm.response.json().content;",
                  "if (c && c.length) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('terminalId', c[0].terminalId);",
                  "  pm.test('PAN is masked in response', () => pm.expect(String(c[0].maskedPan || '')).to.not.match(/^[0-9]{13,19}$/));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pos/transactions?page=0&size=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "pos", "transactions"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20" },
                { "key": "processingStatus", "value": "SETTLED", "disabled": true, "description": "RECEIVED | ACCEPTED | UNMATCHED | COMPLIANCE_HOLD | SETTLEMENT_HELD | GROUPED | SETTLED | DISPUTED | FAILED_RETRYABLE | REJECTED | FAILED" },
                { "key": "dateFrom", "value": "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateTo", "value": "2026-08-31T23:59:59Z", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: GET_POS_TRANSACTIONS. 403 UNAUTHORIZED_USER if missing.\n\nThis request saves the first returned terminalId into {{terminalId}} so the next requests can reuse it."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. GET my transactions by terminal",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('All rows belong to the requested terminal', () => {",
                  "  const c = pm.response.json().content || [];",
                  "  c.forEach(t => pm.expect(t.terminalId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('terminalId')));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pos/transactions/terminals/{{terminalId}}?page=0&size=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "pos", "transactions", "terminals", "{{terminalId}}"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20" },
                { "key": "processingStatus", "value": "SETTLED", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateFrom", "value": "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateTo", "value": "2026-08-31T23:59:59Z", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: GET_POS_TRANSACTIONS + ownership of the terminal.\nA terminal that exists but belongs to another profile raises PosDeviceNotFoundException, NOT a 403 - treat both as access-denied outcomes."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. GET my ledger by terminal",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const c = pm.response.json().content || [];",
                  "if (c.length && c[0].reconBatchRefNum) { pm.collectionVariables.set('batchRef', c[0].reconBatchRefNum); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pos/ledger/terminals/{{terminalId}}?page=0&size=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "pos", "ledger", "terminals", "{{terminalId}}"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20" },
                { "key": "status", "value": "SUCCESS", "disabled": true, "description": "PENDING | SUCCESS | FAILED | REVERSED" },
                { "key": "entryType", "value": "POS_CASH_IN", "disabled": true, "description": "POS_CASH_IN | REVERSAL | SUSPENSE" },
                { "key": "dateFrom", "value": "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateTo", "value": "2026-08-31T23:59:59Z", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: GET_POS_LEDGER + ownership of the terminal."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. GET my ledger by wallet",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pos/ledger/wallets/{{walletReference}}?page=0&size=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "pos", "ledger", "wallets", "{{walletReference}}"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20" },
                { "key": "status", "value": "SUCCESS", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "entryType", "value": "POS_CASH_IN", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateFrom", "value": "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateTo", "value": "2026-08-31T23:59:59Z", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: GET_POS_LEDGER + the wallet must be linked to the caller's profile."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin (back-office, unscoped)",
      "description": "No ownership check - a holder of the privilege sees and acts on every profile's data.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. GET all transactions (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Page envelope', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().content).to.be.an('array'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/pos/transactions?page=0&size=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "pos", "transactions"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20" },
                { "key": "deviceId", "value": "42", "disabled": true, "description": "Long - internal device ID" },
                { "key": "terminalId", "value": "{{terminalId}}", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "walletCode", "value": "{{walletCode}}", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "profileCode", "value": "{{profileCode}}", "disabled": true, "description": "How an admin scopes down to one merchant" },
                { "key": "processingStatus", "value": "SETTLED", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateFrom", "value": "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateTo", "value": "2026-08-31T23:59:59Z", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: ADMIN_GET_POS_TRANSACTIONS. Same DTO as the business list, but unscoped."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. GET all ledger entries (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/pos/ledger?page=0&size=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "pos", "ledger"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20" },
                { "key": "terminalId", "value": "{{terminalId}}", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "walletReference", "value": "{{walletReference}}", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "status", "value": "SUCCESS", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "entryType", "value": "POS_CASH_IN", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateFrom", "value": "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateTo", "value": "2026-08-31T23:59:59Z", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: ADMIN_GET_POS_LEDGER."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. GET all ACH transfers",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const c = pm.response.json().content || [];",
                  "pm.test('allowedActions only on AWAITING_APPROVAL', () => {",
                  "  c.forEach(t => {",
                  "    if (t.status === 'AWAITING_APPROVAL') { pm.expect(t.allowedActions).to.have.members(['RELEASE', 'REJECT']); }",
                  "    else { pm.expect(t.allowedActions || []).to.be.empty; }",
                  "  });",
                  "});",
                  "const pending = c.find(t => t.status === 'AWAITING_APPROVAL');",
                  "if (pending) { pm.collectionVariables.set('batchRef', pending.reconBatchRefNum); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/pos/ach-transfers?page=0&size=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "pos", "ach-transfers"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20", "description": "Server caps the effective page size at 100" },
                { "key": "batchRef", "value": "{{batchRef}}", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "terminalId", "value": "{{terminalId}}", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "walletCode", "value": "{{walletCode}}", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "beneficiaryAccountIban", "value": "SA0000000000000000000000", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "status", "value": "AWAITING_APPROVAL", "disabled": true, "description": "AWAITING_APPROVAL | APPROVED | PENDING | SUCCESSFUL | REVERSED | REJECTED" },
                { "key": "dateFrom", "value": "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "dateTo", "value": "2026-08-31T23:59:59Z", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: ADMIN_GET_POS_ACH_TRANSFERS.\nThis request stores the first AWAITING_APPROVAL batchRef into {{batchRef}} for the release/reject calls below."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. POST release ACH transfers",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Batch counters add up', () => {",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(b.succeeded + b.failed + b.skipped).to.eql(b.total);",
                  "  pm.expect(b.items.length).to.eql(b.total);",
                  "});",
                  "// Per-item outcomes (NOT_FOUND / INVALID_STATUS / ALREADY_RELEASED / FAILED / REJECTED_BY_BANK)",
                  "// are reported inside this 200 body - they are NOT HTTP errors."
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } },
              "raw": "{\n  \"batchRefs\": [\"{{batchRef}}\"],\n  \"reason\": \"Approved by finance for weekly settlement run\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/pos/ach-transfers/release",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "pos", "ach-transfers", "release"]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: ADMIN_RELEASE_POS_ACH_TRANSFERS.\n\nValidation (400 on failure): batchRefs non-null, non-empty, no blank entries, max 100 items; reason max 255 chars.\nOnly AWAITING_APPROVAL transfers can be released - anything else returns INVALID_STATUS inside the 200 body.\n\nCAUTION: this sends a real payment instruction to the bank on whichever environment you point it at."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5. POST reject ACH transfers",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Results limited to REJECTED / NOT_FOUND / INVALID_STATUS', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.json().items.forEach(i => pm.expect(['REJECTED', 'NOT_FOUND', 'INVALID_STATUS']).to.include(i.result));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } },
              "raw": "{\n  \"batchRefs\": [\"{{batchRef}}\"],\n  \"reason\": \"Rejected - beneficiary IBAN under review\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/pos/ach-transfers/reject",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "pos", "ach-transfers", "reject"]
            },
            "description": "Privilege: ADMIN_REJECT_POS_ACH_TRANSFERS. Same request shape and validation rules as release. Only AWAITING_APPROVAL can be rejected."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6. POST release - invalid body (negative)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('ErrorMessageDto shape', () => {",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  const e = Array.isArray(b) ? b[0] : b;",
                  "  pm.expect(e).to.have.property('httpStatusCode');",
                  "  pm.expect(e.message).to.have.property('messageCode');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } },
              "raw": "{\n  \"batchRefs\": [\"\"],\n  \"reason\": \"blank batchRef should fail validation\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/pos/ach-transfers/release",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "pos", "ach-transfers", "release"]
            },
            "description": "Negative test: a blank entry in batchRefs must fail AchTransferActionRequestValidator -> 400.\nOther cases worth trying by editing the body: empty array, null, more than 100 refs, reason longer than 255 chars."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Integration (terminal callback)",
      "description": "Server-to-server MADA terminal callback. Despite being a bank-style webhook it goes through the normal POS gateway route, so it still needs a JWT, device-finger-print and platform - plus Accept-Language, which is a required header on the controller method.\n\nPrivilege: POS_TRANSACTION_CALLBACK.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. POST callback - valid purchase (200 ACCEPTED)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('result is ACCEPTED', () => pm.expect(b.result).to.eql('ACCEPTED'));",
                  "pm.test('subStatus is ACCEPTED or PARKED', () => pm.expect(['ACCEPTED', 'PARKED']).to.include(b.subStatus));",
                  "pm.test('reconciliationKey present', () => pm.expect(b.reconciliationKey).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "if (b.subStatus === 'PARKED') { console.log('Parked - terminal not matched. reasonCode:', b.reasonCode); }",
                  "if (b.externalReference) { pm.collectionVariables.set('externalReference', b.externalReference); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept-Language", "value": "en" },
              { "key": "device-finger-print", "value": "{{deviceFingerPrint}}" },
              { "key": "platform", "value": "{{platform}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } },
              "raw": "{\n  \"madaArchives\": {\n    \"madaTransactionResult\": {\n      \"Retailer\": \"ACME Retail LLC\",\n      \"Performance\": \"OK\",\n      \"BankId\": \"01\",\n      \"MerchantId\": \"{{merchantId}}\",\n      \"TerminalId\": \"{{terminalId}}\",\n      \"Mcc\": \"5411\",\n      \"Stan\": \"{{stan}}\",\n      \"Version\": \"1.0\",\n      \"Rrn\": \"{{rrn}}\",\n      \"CardScheme\": \"MADA\",\n      \"ApplicationLabel\": \"MADA\",\n      \"Pan\": \"410621******1234\",\n      \"CardExpiryDate\": \"2812\",\n      \"TransactionType\": \"PURCHASE\",\n      \"Amount\": { \"Amount\": 150.00 },\n      \"Result\": \"APPROVED\",\n      \"CardholderVerification\": \"PIN\",\n      \"ApprovalCode\": \"654321\",\n      \"EmvTags\": {\n        \"PosEntryMode\": \"051\",\n        \"ResponseCode\": \"00\",\n        \"TerminalStatusCode\": \"00\",\n        \"AID\": \"A0000000041010\",\n        \"TVR\": \"0000008000\",\n        \"TSI\": \"E800\",\n        \"CVR\": \"0000000000\",\n        \"ACI\": \"Y\",\n        \"AC\": \"1234567890ABCDEF\",\n        \"KID\": \"01\",\n        \"PAR\": \"\",\n        \"FPAN\": \"\"\n      },\n      \"Campaign\": { \"QrCodeData\": \"\", \"CampaignText\": \"\" }\n    }\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pos/transactions/callback",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "pos", "transactions", "callback"]
            },
            "description": "Stan and Rrn are randomised by the collection pre-request script, so each send is a new transaction.\n\nExpected outcomes:\n- Terminal matched and active -> 200, subStatus ACCEPTED\n- Terminal unknown -> still 200, subStatus PARKED, reasonCode UNKNOWN_TID"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. POST callback - duplicate replay (idempotency)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Replay stays ACCEPTED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().result).to.eql('ACCEPTED'));",
                  "// Send this request twice. TerminalId + Rrn + Stan are pinned here, so the second send",
                  "// must be handled as an idempotent DUPLICATE - no second transaction row."
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
